"""hearth-colibri: Colibri, the second AI engine in Server mode next to Ollama (docs/SERVER-MODE.md, "Colibri").

Colibri (https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri, Apache-2.0, by Vincenzo Fornaro) runs very large mixture-of-experts
models on a normal PC: the hot experts on the graphics card, warm ones in RAM, cold ones streamed from the NVMe drive.
It speaks the OpenAI API (/v1/chat/completions, /v1/models) and Anthropic's (/v1/messages).

Nothing of it is in the image and nothing is downloaded until you ask:
  - the engine: Colibri's own release COLIBRI_TAG (about 14 MB), its SHA-256 checked against the one Hearth pins AND
    the release's SHA256SUMS.txt, its archive checked, unpacked into ~/.local/share/hearth/colibri/engine (as you);
  - each model: only the one you pick, by Colibri's own setup (coli setup: resumable, every file checked against its
    checksum), into your models folder (~/colibri-models unless you choose another drive), after a free-space check.
It runs as your own user service hearth-colibri.service (no [Install]; its timer is enabled only while it's on, like
AI pictures), on 127.0.0.1:COLIBRI_PORT and, while Tailscale is up, this PC's Tailscale address only (that port is
in Hearth's Tailscale-only firewall rule while it's on). Light mode stops it while you play (it holds the graphics
card) and starts it again after. If it fails, nothing else is touched: Ollama, Server mode and Game Mode go on.

  hearth-colibri status              JSON for Settings and the dashboard (reads only; writes nothing)
  hearth-colibri catalog             every model Colibri's catalog offers (coli setup --list --all --json), each with
                                     its download size, the disk it needs and an honest fit / speed for this PC
  hearth-colibri plan ID             a downloaded model's real plan on this PC (coli plan --json, coli doctor --json)
  hearth-colibri install             the engine, in its own unit (only when you ask); install-run is that unit
  hearth-colibri download ID         one model, in its own unit, after a free-space check; download-run is that unit
  hearth-colibri cancel              stop a download (what's there stays: running it again continues)
  hearth-colibri use ID              the model Colibri serves (a downloaded one); restarts it if it's running
  hearth-colibri set KEY VALUE       engine (ollama|colibri|both: Settings › Home server's switches), default
                                     (ollama|colibri: what Hearth's AI pieces use first), modelsDir (a folder)
  hearth-colibri remove-model ID sure   delete a downloaded model's files
  hearth-colibri remove              the engine goes (your models stay)
  hearth-colibri run                 hearth-colibri.service: coli serve for the model you picked
  hearth-colibri folders             where models could go (your Home and your drives, with free space)

Settings are ai-engines.json's (hearth_ai_engines.py) and home-server.json's (on / pause), never a copy here. Install
and download progress is state: ~/.local/state/nimbus/colibri.json. Output: one JSON line; failures print
"error: ..." and exit 1. Nothing here goes through a shell.
"""
